import IEANTN.Vocabulary

/-!
# Node `KLN.v1`

An explicit zero density estimate: a bound on the number of zeros of the Riemann zeta function in
a rectangle to the right of the critical line. Together with a zero-free region, this is one of
the two analytic inputs the Chebyshev-function bounds rest on.

**This node states nothing yet.** It records that the paper is in scope and carries its
citation, so that a conclusion can be added the moment a downstream node needs one.

What to add first:

The density estimate itself, in a form that names its parameters, so that the nodes consuming it
can instantiate rather than re-derive.
-/
